% cook_domain — a cook of the shared-pot kitchen (specialist-tree s-404d001f step 3a; steps/step3-cases-brief.md):
% two cooks, ONE pot. The cook works its own orders with its own hand (fetch an onion, a dish; serve) and asks
% for the pot when it holds an onion (tick__want, a report of the protocol module). The pot's rules read the
% grant themselves ($tick__grant(S, pot): the manifest's gating: program), so a cook without the pot keeps its
% onion and its request: its state is never ahead of the world. After plating it gives the pot back
% (tick__release) — its own copy of the grant consumed, so a grant the director has not revoked yet (the
% hysteresis) is never used for the next soup: that needs a new request and a new grant — reports done
% (tick__done) and serves. kitchen.llp's recipe (three onions make a soup), per cook.
% A cook is a PATH member (specialist-tree step 3c, the architect's ruling (c)): calm is its idle, the triggers
% that consume it (ask_pot; ask_plate, for a soup of its own already cooking) are its begin and report
% tick__active, plating reports tick__done. A stop (the director's tick__cancel) drops its engagement, never the
% world's soup or onions (the generated cancels below: metis.catalog.protocol_stub); a cook whose order still
% stands asks again at its next tick with a fresh ticket. A kitchen halts when its orders are withdrawn.
catalog cook_domain 1.
provenance text "a cook of the shared-pot kitchen: its own hand, the one pot by request and grant" "2026-10-25".
include "iface/protocol_domain.llp".
layers (dyn).
stages (act).
namespace cook produce (dyn).

% ── the kitchen as this cook reads it (world-private: its own copy, synced by its own host) ──
pred hand_free : cook.
pred held_onion : cook.
pred held_dish : cook.
pred held_soup : cook.
pred pot_space : cook.                    % room in the pot (one atom per onion it takes)
pred pot_onion : cook.                    % onions in the pot
pred cooking : cook.                      % a soup cooks in the pot
%% The order this cook is working to: the dish it serves.
pred order : cook.                        % one of this cook's orders waiting

% ── the cook's own ──
bwd self(domain).                         % which cook this is (the instance's fact)
pred calm(domain) : cook.                 % no request out: the cook's idle (the protocol stub's)
pred asked(domain) : cook.                % its request is out: until it gives the pot back (its engagement)
pred mine(domain) : cook.                 % the soup cooking is this cook's: the soup's, kept through a stop

stage act {
  %% I take an onion for my order.
  fetch_onion [dyn] : $order * hand_free * $pot_space -o held_onion.
  %% I need the pot: I ask for it.
  ask_pot [dyn] : $order * $held_onion * $self(S) * calm(S) -o asked(S) * tick__want(S, pot) * tick__active(S).
  %% My soup cooks and I have no request out (a stop cancelled it): I ask for the pot to plate it.
  ask_plate [dyn] : $order * $mine(S) * $self(S) * calm(S) -o asked(S) * tick__want(S, pot) * tick__active(S).
  % >>> generated by metis.catalog.protocol_stub: the stop's cancels (regenerate, do not edit)
  %% Stopped: I drop my goal.
  cancel [dyn] : tick__cancel(S) * $self(S) * asked(S) -o calm(S).
  %% Stopped as I finished: nothing left to drop.
  cancel_none [dyn] : calm(S) * tick__cancel(S) * $self(S) -o calm(S).   % the race: its done and the stop in one director beat (path_pop, stop_cancel: the sampled order)
  % <<< generated
  %% The pot is mine: I put my onion in.
  load [dyn] : held_onion * pot_space * $self(S) * $asked(S) * $tick__grant(S, pot) -o hand_free * pot_onion.
  %% Three onions are in: I start the soup.
  start [dyn] : $hand_free * pot_onion * pot_onion * pot_onion * $self(S) * $asked(S) * $tick__grant(S, pot) -o cooking * mine(S).
  %% My soup cooks: I take a dish.
  fetch_dish [dyn] : $order * hand_free * $mine(S) * $self(S) -o held_dish.
  %% My soup is done: I plate it and give the pot back.
  plate [dyn] : held_dish * cooking * mine(S) * asked(S) * $self(S) * tick__grant(S, pot) -o held_soup * pot_space * pot_space * pot_space * tick__release(S, pot) * tick__done(S) * calm(S).   % the pot emptied: room for three; its copy of the grant given up with it (the next soup needs a new grant)
  %% I serve my order.
  serve [dyn] : held_soup * order * $self(S) -o hand_free.
}
